// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2946194412" "You've arrested all the psychics that Praetor Tilman named."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3282150633" "Mother is <i>so</i> proud of you, {HeroName}. I was watching your progress the <i>entire</i> time. The <i>nerve</i> of those Syndicate to <i>criticize</i> me, to <i>slander</i> my name like that! They have no shame, no nobility, no <i>class</i>! When I'm through with them, oh, they <i>will</i> learn to respect Praetoria and its people, <i>believe</i> me, {HeroName}.<br><br><color orange>Praetor Tilman lets out a pleased sigh, calming herself.</color><br><br>But... let's speak of some other things, yes? I sensed a very... <i>powerful</i> force in that office building with you. A psychic force that <i>should not</i> be allowed to run wild, to roam <i>outside</i> of my... <i>tender</i> care. I intend to hunt this force down, {HeroName}, for the <i>good</i> of all Praetoria. After all, do we <i>really</i> want a force out there that could be as powerful as me, <i>without</i> having the <i>care</i> that I do for you all? No... no, we don't."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Beholder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro1 Text :
"P3429390315" "<i>You</i>! {HeroName}! How... how could you? You and I... we once fought together. You know of my condition... And now you're going to <i>deliver</i> me back to Mother? Why? Why?! Why can't you just let me <i>die</i> in peace, let me die killing those that turned me into this?!"
// Answer Text :
"P1159648104" "We all have to pay for what we've done, Beholder. Now's your time."
// Page YourTime Text :
"P1248378585" "<color orange>Beholder laughs, coughing hard.</color><br><br>I thought we were comrades, {HeroName}. You knew my fight against Mother. Knew that I longed for freedom. And now... here we are. You... you stand to bring me in, for <i>her</i>. You know the short time I have left on this miserable planet... and you would have me spend it locked in Mother's cold embrace.<br><br>I can't let that happen, {HeroName}. I never wanted to hurt you. But you're leaving me no choice. One of us... one of us isn't walking away from this today."
// Answer Text :
"P821503013" "Don't do anything you're going to regret, Beholder."
// Page FinalPage Text :
"P195868228" "The others will deal with you now!"
// Answer Text :
"P3682174071" "Hmph...!"
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P1392614893" "<color orange>Beholder looks up at you with a weakened plea.</color><br><br>Don't let... don't let Mother take me back. I don't want to go back, I <i>don't</i>. She made me this way... She <i>stole</i> my life, just to have her own pleasures. She MADE me into this... I used to be happy, used to be <i>normal</i>! Just don't send me back to that place, that <i>nightmare</i>!"
// Answer Text :
"P915638138" "And the people you've hurt? What about them?"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P2219618363" "They <i>deserve</i> it for putting up with a government that allows filth like Mother! They could stand and fight with us, but they let it go. And for that, they need to <i>suffer</i> until they get the message. Tilman is a <i>beast</i> who deserves nothing but death!<br><br>I won't stop until I get my vengeance... you have to let me go, you have to let me continue my fight against her! Against the people!"
// Answer Text :
"P1840434791" "You and I are enemies, as long as you continue hurting innocents for your cause."
// Page ChoiceAPage2 Text :
"P2422337044" "Then the <i>others</i> will deal with you!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1329871790" "Sometimes, {HeroName}, those <i>scoundrels</i> in the Resistance manage to kidnap my <i>dear</i> girls and break them off from my tender embrace. You would never want to be torn from my care, would you, {HeroName}? I would <i>never</i> treat you poorly, of course. But some people, they <i>insist</i> on believing that I am some sort... some sort of <i>monster</i>! Lies, hate, <i>anger</i> is poured into their minds, into their very souls, poisoning their thoughts about me. I can see them, feel them, and then... <i>darkness</i>, as if they are no longer there. But Mother... Mother will <i>not</i> stand for her girls leaving her side, {HeroName}.<br><br>There is one such girl, she was <i>such</i> a good dear when she was one of my little ones. But now, she goes by the name <color yellow>Beholder</color>, a part of those <i>terrorists</i> in the Resistance. I have spent some time trying to track her and the man who kidnapped her from my grasp, <color yellow>Hatchet</color>.<br><br>And now... I have found them. Trapped like <i>rats</i> in the tunnels. And you... {HeroName}... I want you to bring them to <i>justice</i> for all that they've done."
// AcceptString :
"P3573967697" "What are their crimes?"
// SendOffString :
"P3525623050" "You need to know more of their crimes, other than the fact that the man forced one of my <i>own daughters</i> from my side? You would <i>doubt</i> me?!<br><br>Mmm... I apologize, {HeroName}. It is a very... sour subject, yes? Mother does not mean to yell at you. I never do. Their crimes are <i>many</i>. My... sad, former daughter, <i>Beholder</i>, has wired many of my little girls to have <i>psychic explosions</i>. She betrays her <i>own</i> sisters out of some... some <i>anger</i> towards me! Do you know how many of my girls have died because of her, how many people in Praetoria have suffered? Too many, {HeroName}!<br><br>Here is the location of her and her <i>little</i> man, Hatchet. I want you to bring them in. Show them that Mother is always willing to bring one of her daughters back into her flock, but is <i>not</i> tolerant of those who would <i>strike</i> at her family."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1687663246" "Bring in Hatchet and Beholder"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2415327156" "Please, {HeroName}, do not keep Mother waiting. I've spent too long yearning to have my little girl back in my arms."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1606793721" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Running Away</color>"

